  "what_this_fix_does_NOT_resolve": [
    "The paper's kappa collapse 0.253 (v1) -> 0.0072 (v2corpus), TANITAD_PAPER.md:1867-1868. It is built from man_pred vs traj_dir and never touches man_tgt, so this fix leaves it exactly where DIRYAW_REREAD 1.3 left it: CONFOUNDED with the label-definition change, and stacked on a genuinely degenerate head (maneuver_dir = 8 left / 6 straight / 404 right = 96.65 % one class, MEASURED from the banked panel).",
    "The nav/route label family. hierarchy.py's rl.nav_command / rl.route_target are still unconditional v1 while THREE route label versions exist (v1, v2 via cfg.v2_labels, v2.1 via cfg.v21_route_labels). Deliberately NOT fixed: one boolean cannot express three versions and guessing would be a new defect.",
    "four_families.tactical's factor_from_kinematics call omits kappa, which selects refc_tactical's v1 branch. Both raters share that gate so it is self-consistent \u2014 a label-DEFINITION question, not a head-scored-against-labels-it-never-saw defect. Reported, not changed."
  ],
